---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/service.css";

const SITE = "https://www.tmdesignengineering.com";
const url = `${SITE}/services/contract-engineering`;
const faqs = [
  ["How do you charge for contract work?", "I charge a day rate for ongoing capacity, a retainer for regular availability, or a fixed price for a defined deliverable, so depending on your needs I can offer you the most value."],
  ["Remote or on-site?", "Both. I'm based in Edinburgh and work remotely with teams anywhere. I like to be on-site for kick-offs, factory visits or prototype demonstrations, and I'm happy to travel for important meetings."],
  ["How quickly can you start?", "I'm set up to start immediately after agreeing a contract, though my availability varies as consultancy work is my main source."],
  ["How do you handle IP and NDAs?", "Your IP is yours; I work under your NDA and contracts as standard, and I'm used to the IP and confidentiality expectations of consumer hardware companies."],
  ["Do you take long or short engagements?", "Both, anything from a month to ongoing support across a project, retainer style. Whatever the shape, you get senior engineering that slots into how your team already works."],
];
const jsonld = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    "@id": `${url}#service`,
    serviceType: "Contract design engineering",
    name: "Contract Engineering",
    description: "Specialist or extra design engineering capacity for product teams, mechanical, firmware-mechanical crossover, thermal and design for manufacture, remote or on-site, on a day rate, retainer or fixed-price basis.",
    provider: { "@id": `${SITE}/#business` },
    areaServed: ["United Kingdom", "Worldwide"],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Contract Engineering", item: url },
    ],
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ "@type": "Question", name: q, acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: a } })),
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Contract Design Engineering, Extra Capacity for Product Teams | Thomas McKee"
  description="Experienced design engineering on demand for product teams: mechanical, firmware-mechanical crossover, thermal and DFM, remote or on-site, on a day rate, retainer or fixed-price basis."
  type="website"
  jsonld={jsonld}>
<main>
  <section class="svc-hero">
    <div class="wrap svc-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Service · Contract Engineering</span>
        <h1>Experienced design engineering, <em>on demand.</em></h1>
        <p class="lede">Specialist or extra engineering capacity for teams that have a specific project or problem, or that need quick extra resource. An experienced design engineer who can drop into a project and deliver quickly, across mechanical design, firmware-and-mechanical crossover, thermal analysis and design for manufacture, remotely or on-site, for as long as you need.</p>
        <div class="svc-hero-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#contact">Discuss a contract <span class="arw">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#fit">How I fit in</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="spec" aria-label="Service summary">
        <div class="spec-head"><span>Service Spec</span><span>CE-06</span></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Engage</div><div class="spec-v">Day rate · retainer · fixed</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Mode</div><div class="spec-v">Remote or on-site</div></div>
        <div class="spec-row"><div class="spec-k">Areas</div><div class="spec-v">Mech · application firmware · thermal · DFM</div></div>
        <div class="spec-note">For defined engineering work where you already know what's needed, or for fast extra resource able to drop into a team.</div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Who it's for</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">For product teams that need a safe pair of hands</h2>
      <div class="pain" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)">
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"We need a specialist in a certain area, or experienced capacity, fast."</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"We're a design consultancy and need engineering expertise on a certain project or across a range."</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"We've hit a hard problem, thermal, firmware-mechanical, DFM, that we don't have the resource in house to solve."</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"We want someone who has actually shipped consumer hardware at volume."</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="fit">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">How I fit in</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Senior engineering, working with your team</h2>
      <div class="deliv">
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">01</div><h3>Project lead capacity</h3><p>I'm happy bridging the gap between mechanical, firmware and electronic development, and can manage the separate workstreams and the integration between them.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">02</div><h3>Specialist depth</h3><p>With expertise in mechanical design, firmware-and-mechanical crossover, thermal analysis and design for manufacture, if you need a specialist on a certain project I can jump in immediately.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">03</div><h3>Working with you</h3><p>I'm flexible, working in your tools, cadences and processes, remotely or on-site, so I can have an impact on projects from the first day.</p></div>
        <div class="di"><div class="dn">04</div><h3>Production experience</h3><p>Having worked with different manufacturers in the UK and China, remotely and in person, I have managed the relationships, worked with a range of capabilities, and taken products through tooling and volume manufacture, actually being there as they were built.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Why me</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Shipped award-winning products at various volumes</h2>
      <div class="proof">
        <div class="pl">Track record</div>
        <p>Over four years at Ooni I developed premium consumer products end to end: award-winning, with patented and patent-pending inventions, and sold worldwide. With a proactive attitude to solving problems, I can jump into new scenarios and provide instant value. That is how I took on the firmware development lead role on a Red Dot award-winning product as a mechanical engineer by trade. Being able to work across the whole picture, with cross-discipline expertise, is how I can be effective immediately across a range of problems.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-cred">
        <span class="ci"><b>4+ years</b> shipping premium consumer hardware at Ooni</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>Firmware &amp; mechanical</b> crossover · <b>thermal</b> and high-temperature work</span>
        <span class="ci">Products <b>sold worldwide</b>, Red Dot &amp; iF award-winning</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Common questions</h2>
      <div class="faq">
        {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (
          <div class="fitem"><div class="fq">{q}</div><div class="fa">{a}</div></div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band alt" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta">
        <div class="inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Let's talk</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Need experienced engineering capacity?</h2>
          <p>Tell me what you need, the timeline and how your team works, and we can discuss the engagement model that suits you best, how I can help, how quickly I can start, and what it costs.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/#contact">Discuss a contract <span class="arw">→</span></a>
            <span class="price-tag">Day rate · retainer · fixed scope</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
</Base>
